<title>USA: Urohealth sees $25.5 mln charge in Q2. [Corrected 19:12 gmt]</title>
<headline>Urohealth sees $25.5 mln charge in Q2. [Corrected 19:12 gmt]</headline>
<dateline>NEWPORT BEACH, Calif. 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects value of charge from $22.5 mln)</p>
<p>Urohealth Systems Inc said Wednesday it will take a one-time charge $25.5 million in the second quarter ending September 30 to write down incomplete research and development costs associated with its acquisition of Richard-Allen Medical.</p>
<p>The company said it also expects about $4 million in restructuring charges in the second quarter related with the closing of the Richard-Allen deal and others.  </p>
<p>Seperately, the company said it has entered a $35 million credity facility with Banque Indosuez Belgique SA structured as a $20 million term loan and a $15 million revolver.</p>
</text>
